# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# This file did not exist until the credential-exposure pass. Its absence is
# how a production JS bundle containing a live read-write database token got
# committed into the Android release source set and pushed to a public remote.
# The per-directory .gitignore files remain, and are narrower on purpose;
# these rules are the backstop that applies everywhere.

# ─── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
# ~220 MB of vendored dependencies was committed here once and is permanently
# in this repository's history.
node_modules_bak/

# ─── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a real credential. If you generate a key locally, confirm it is
# ignored BEFORE it lands on disk.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.keystore
!GroceryApp/android/app/debug.keystore
*.mobileprovision

# ─── Build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The React Native bundle is regenerated by the Gradle `react { }` block on
# every release build (it shells out to @expo/cli `export:embed`), so there is
# never a reason to track it. The exact filename is listed as well as the
# glob, because android/.gitignore's `*.jsbundle` does not match
# `index.android.bundle` — that gap is the original defect.
index.android.bundle
index.ios.bundle
*.jsbundle
*.bundle.map

# Hermes bytecode. Plain `grep` does not find strings inside these; `strings`
# does, which is how a token was found in one.
*.hbc

# Expo export output
GroceryApp/dist-android/
GroceryApp/dist-ios/
dist/
.expo/
web-build/

# Native build output
build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
DerivedData/
*.hprof

# ─── OS / editor junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.orig.*
*.swp
*~
.idea/
*.iml

# ─── Local debugging leftovers ──────────────────────────────────────────────
current_screen.png
window_dump.xml
